#X text 624 38 Per-Creature Volume and Mute: Each creature sound (SMALL.wav \, SEASHELL.wav \, LONG.wav) has its own volume fader and mute switch \, and is sent to its own DAC output (1 \, 2 \, and 3 respectively). Turning a track's volume fader up or down changes the level sent to that track's DAC output \, its VU-meter \, and the headphone mix \, all at once. Muting a track silences only its DAC output. The VU-meter keeps showing the track's current level \, and the track still contributes to the headphone mix \, even while muted. Use mute to silence a speaker without losing your ability to monitor that track or hear it in headphones. ___________________________________________________________ Headphone Mix: All three tracks are summed together \, using their fader levels but ignoring mute status \, into a single mono signal. This mix has its own volume control and is sent identically to both headphone outputs (DAC 5 and 6).;
